On Fri, 30 Sep 2005 20:25:39 -0700, pdpi wrote:
> It seems my archeologists have a sadly low survivability index. None ever
> get past dlvl3-4. Now, some questions warrant being asked.

I just ascended my first archaologist; maybe I can help answer some.

> Why is it that people advise you to use the pickaxe (1d6 damage, 3.5 avg/1
> min) instead of the +2 whip (3.5 avg/3 min), except where it pertains to
> thick-skinned monsters?

Because the big pick that dwarves sometimes carry (and dig with) is
apparently an awesome weapon - and the same class as pickaxe.  Actually, I
ended up using the pickaxe as my weapon through a good chunk of the early
game; it was only when I stumbled upon grayswandir in a shop that I
switched over (see post "Woot!") :)

> How do you deal with the low strength? Pushing boulders around is a
> massively boring activity that also tends to make your food supply run
> low.

Don't carry much :-D  Lots of caches, I think, and not needing to lug
every scroll around. Seriously, I never even noticed how low my strength
was; by the time I got around to the run, it was just over 18/04, IIRC...

> How is it that people tend to get their hands on silver sabres? I never
> seem to find any.

Watch Captain in minetown seems to be the preferred way.  Big pets to take
him out help.  If you're lawful, sacrifice (or wish) for grayswandir. 
They're generated sometimes, but they're kinda rare, I think...

> Besides these specific issues, is there any sort of global strategy to
> follow regaring archeologists?

Be *very* careful with them.  They have to potential to become super
shredding machines, but until they've reached a decent kit, they're very
vulnerable.  At least that's how it seemed to me, when mine were
dropping like flies...

Treat them as a weak character - run away a lot, use
pets, throw daggers.  If you're capable of pulling off protection racket,
that can work if you can ID some gems... (think of it as playing a
pacifist for 4-5 levels).  But don't think you can go toe-to-toe with big
mosters. Also, IIRC, archeologists are fast, so use that to your
advantage.  Run loops around monsters; make them come to you - preferrable
through your pets and a hail of daggers.

Hope that helps!

